<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Apple's privacy manifest. Required at upload, and for this app it is short
  for a real reason rather than because corners were cut.

  NSPrivacyTracking = false and no tracking domains: nothing here follows anyone
  across apps or sites. There is no analytics SDK, no advertising identifier and
  no third-party network call from the app at all — every request goes to
  cubewithin.com, which is our own server.

  NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is EMPTY, and that is the honest answer, not a
  convenient one. What a person writes is published by them, to a public sky,
  under a name they invent; it is not collected about them. There is no account,
  no email address, no phone number, no contacts, no location, no photos, no
  device identifier sent anywhere. What identifies an author is a random string
  the phone generates for itself, which the server only ever sees as a SHA-256
  hash — it maps to no person, and nobody, including us, can look a person up
  by it.

  The one API below needs declaring because iOS counts it as "required reason":

    UserDefaults (CA92.1) — Capacitor Preferences keeps the author secret and
    the display name here, and both are read only by this app. CA92.1 is the
    reason code for exactly that: data accessible only to the app itself.

  If anything is ever added that measures people — a crash reporter, an
  analytics SDK, anything with an SDK key — this file has to change in the same
  commit. A manifest that quietly stops being true is worse than none.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
  <false/>

  <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
  <array/>

  <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
  <array/>

  <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
      <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
      <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
      <array>
        <string>CA92.1</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
